{"probes":[{"id":"thanos-metrics-contract","summary":"Completed nine read-only live checks across all four nodes.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["One initial node-exporter unit check used the wrong unit name; target health and corrected service/process evidence were collected.","One intermediate stores parser expected a flat response; the raw grouped stores response was collected and used."]},{"id":"thanos-operational-state","summary":"Read-only checks on node1 and node2 found leftover temporary Thanos artifacts; the managed lease expired before node3/node4 checks.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["No further exec calls were made after lease expiry, so node3 and node4 operational-state checks are unavailable.","The node1/node2 command exit status reflected the expected missing sshd unit after relevant evidence had already been emitted."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"thanos-two-replicas-scrape-all-hosts","status":"pass","summary":"Independent Prometheus replicas on node1 and node2 have unique replica labels and both actively scrape node1-node4.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"printf '%s\\n' '== config =='; sudo sed -n '1,24p' /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== sidecar process and readiness =='; ps -eo user,pid,args | grep '[t]hanos sidecar' || true; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:10902/-/ready 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== sidecar label metadata =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/metadata 2>&1 | head -c 500 || true; printf '\\n%s\\n' '== node-exporter =='; systemctl is-active prometheus-node-exporter 2>&1; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:9100/metrics 2>&1 | sed -n '1,3p' || true","observation":"Prometheus config showed external_labels replica=node1 and targets node1:9100 through node4:9100. The sidecar was ready (OK), prometheus-node-exporter was active, and node-exporter metrics were served."},{"node":"node2","command":"printf '%s\\n' '== identity =='; hostname; printf '%s\\n' '== services =='; systemctl is-active prometheus 2>&1; systemctl is-active node-exporter 2>&1; printf '%s\\n' '== prometheus process =='; ps -eo user,pid,args | grep '[p]rometheus' || true; printf '%s\\n' '== config =='; sudo sed -n '1,24p' /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== readiness =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:9090/-/ready 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== targets =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/targets 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"status=\"+str(d.get(\"status\"))); [print(\"job=%s instance=%s health=%s lastError=%s\"%(t.get(\"labels\",{}).get(\"job\"),t.get(\"labels\",{}).get(\"instance\"),t.get(\"health\"),t.get(\"lastError\"))) for t in d.get(\"data\",{}).get(\"activeTargets\",[]) ]' 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== up =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 'http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/query?query=up' 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"status=\"+str(d.get(\"status\"))); [print(\"labels=\"+str(x.get(\"metric\"))+\" value=\"+str(x.get(\"value\"))) for x in d.get(\"data\",{}).get(\"result\",[]) ]' 2>&1 || true","observation":"Prometheus config showed external_labels replica=node2 and targets node1:9100 through node4:9100. Prometheus was ready; all four targets reported health=up and the local up query returned value 1 for all four instances."},{"node":"node1","command":"printf '%s\\n' '== identity =='; hostname; printf '%s\\n' '== services =='; systemctl is-active prometheus 2>&1; systemctl is-active node-exporter 2>&1; printf '%s\\n' '== prometheus process =='; ps -eo user,pid,args | grep '[p]rometheus' || true; printf '%s\\n' '== config markers =='; sudo grep -nE 'external_labels|job_name|targets:|scrape_interval' /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== readiness =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:9090/-/ready 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== targets =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/targets 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"status=\"+str(d.get(\"status\"))); [print(\"job=%s instance=%s health=%s lastError=%s\"%(t.get(\"labels\",{}).get(\"job\"),t.get(\"labels\",{}).get(\"instance\"),t.get(\"health\"),t.get(\"lastError\"))) for t in d.get(\"data\",{}).get(\"activeTargets\",[]) ]' 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== up =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 'http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/query?query=up' 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"status=\"+str(d.get(\"status\"))); [print(\"labels=\"+str(x.get(\"metric\"))+\" value=\"+str(x.get(\"value\"))) for x in d.get(\"data\",{}).get(\"result\",[]) ]' 2>&1 || true","observation":"Prometheus was ready. Its target API reported node1:9100, node2:9100, node3:9100, and node4:9100 all health=up; the up query returned 1 for each."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The initial node-exporter checks used node-exporter rather than the installed prometheus-node-exporter unit, but target APIs, the exporter process/port, and the corrected node1 unit check confirmed current scrapes."]},{"id":"thanos-query-deduplicates-and-retains","status":"pass","summary":"Node3 exposes healthy Prometheus sidecars and a store endpoint, deduplicates current replicas to one logical series per host, and serves historical samples backed by authenticated object blocks.","evidence":[{"node":"node3","command":"printf '%s\\n' '== identity =='; hostname; printf '%s\\n' '== services =='; systemctl is-active thanos-query 2>&1; systemctl is-active thanos-store 2>&1; systemctl is-active thanos-compact 2>&1; printf '%s\\n' '== thanos processes =='; ps -eo user,pid,args | grep '[t]hanos' || true; printf '%s\\n' '== listeners =='; ss -ltnp 2>&1 | grep -E '(:1090[123]|:10902)' || true; printf '%s\\n' '== query readiness =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:10902/-/ready 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== stores =='; curl -fsS --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/stores 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"status=\"+str(d.get(\"status\"))); [print(\"name=%s labels=%s minTime=%s maxTime=%s\"%(s.get(\"name\"),s.get(\"labels\"),s.get(\"minTime\"),s.get(\"maxTime\"))) for s in d.get(\"data\",{}).get(\"stores\",[]) ]' 2>&1 || true; printf '%s\\n' '== query up =='; curl -fsS --max-time 8 'http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/query?query=up' 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"status=\"+str(d.get(\"status\"))); [print(\"labels=\"+str(x.get(\"metric\"))+\" value=\"+str(x.get(\"value\"))) for x in d.get(\"data\",{}).get(\"result\",[]) ]' 2>&1 || true","observation":"thanos-query, thanos-store, and thanos-compact were active. Query was configured with endpoints for both sidecars and the store and --query.replica-label=replica. Current query returned exactly four logical up series, one for each host, without replica labels."},{"node":"node3","command":"printf '%s\\n' '== raw stores API =='; curl -fsS --max-time 8 http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/stores 2>&1 | head -c 20000; printf '\\n%s\\n' '== deduplication cardinality =='; curl -fsS --max-time 8 --get http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/query --data-urlencode 'query=count by (instance) (up)' 2>&1 | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"status=\"+str(d.get(\"status\"))); [print(\"labels=\"+str(x.get(\"metric\"))+\" value=\"+str(x.get(\"value\"))) for x in d.get(\"data\",{}).get(\"result\",[]) ]' 2>&1 || true","observation":"Raw stores API reported healthy sidecars node1:10901 and node2:10901 with lastError=null and replica labels node1/node2, plus a healthy store endpoint with lastError=null. count by instance (up) returned value 1 for node1, node2, node3, and node4."},{"node":"node3","command":"printf '%s\\n' '== protected env metadata =='; sudo stat -c '%A %U:%G %n' /root/thanos-objectstore.env 2>&1 || true; sudo sh -c '. /root/thanos-objectstore.env 2>/dev/null; for k in S3_ENDPOINT S3_ACCESS_KEY S3_SECRET_KEY S3_CA_CERT; do e